{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "03MP", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-fpqc}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e65aaf926af22380c084432f07ad3de7e72e0601b459713a52b710b2b72db352", "source_text": "Fpqc topology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e96aaba4425ffd4d49d3efabad2bda6b469d44a6c3553a348eb875ddf522eb72", "unit_id": "tag:03MP:title"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03MP", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-section-fpqc}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-descent-proposition-fpqc-descent-quasi-coherent}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:eabf2419adeed52a9976e747bd22249b601fb8c231b0d9a1dd47e9969900d7fc", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe briefly discuss the notion of an fpqc covering of algebraic spaces.\nPlease compare with\nTopologies, Section <REF_0001>.\nWe will show in\nDescent on Spaces,\nProposition <REF_0002>\nthat quasi-coherent sheaves descent along these.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:582772e3b5ed2dfcbc34fcf59679e52fc1995026eeb275dcb8fea959a8010985", "unit_id": "tag:03MP:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03MP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$f_i$", "MATH_0007": "$Z$", "MATH_0008": "$h : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{g_j : Z_j \\to Z\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{X_i \\times_X Z \\to Z\\}_{i \\in I}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-fpqc-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1f9aba0bd17ecb5753e0a1f751dbab4e6a303651871a72d53366f85583106fa7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8f169f9befea9367281fb51ea04e29c16f827ed624a41990e91364e4e088829b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme, and let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nAn <TEXTITOPEN_0001>fpqc covering of <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family of morphisms\n<MATH_0005> of algebraic spaces\nsuch that each <MATH_0006> is flat and such that for every affine scheme\n<MATH_0007> and morphism <MATH_0008> there exists a standard fpqc covering\n<MATH_0009> which refines the family\n<MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2b54e0f09e2c735dcd7f10bd0d2897d4026b26a8b342ca89fb94787856839d37", "unit_id": "tag:03MQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03MP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i_1, \\ldots, i_m \\in I$", "MATH_0002": "$h_j : Z_j \\to X_{i_j}$", "MATH_0003": "$f_{i_j} \\circ h_j = h \\circ g_j$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$X_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-lemma-fpqc-covering-affines-mapping-in}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:331273af690387174ecce2dacb83f015acc66a418383d82d6de9e02ec99ee480", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d2ebc3241a2926bdf703aad8f940d5ccbcef028803b8309195b9b82cbefb3a12", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn other words, there exists indices <MATH_0001> and\nmorphisms <MATH_0002> such that\n<MATH_0003>. Note that if <MATH_0004> and all <MATH_0005> are\nrepresentable, this is the same as a fpqc covering of schemes by\nTopologies, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:46f80043732c892c1881fa9015b949d5cfed338f50d1aa41f0e5d56425c0145f", "unit_id": "tag:03MP:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03MP", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth-syntomic-fppf-fpqc}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a5527bc475360731252ca1aea2938d3c58bf79c43ac3aa647ae56f898d01285a", "source_text": "Any fppf covering is an fpqc covering, and a fortiori,\nany syntomic, smooth, <ACCENT_0001>tale or Zariski covering is an fpqc covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d73450f56026c64efca52e9901ba13d9900cba0e71e0c9c9a0f52b0bf37ad7d8", "unit_id": "tag:0DFQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03MP", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\{f_i : U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$f_i$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\to U$", "MATH_0005": "$V$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{V_{ij} \\to V \\times_U U_i\\}$", "MATH_0007": "$V_{ij}$", "MATH_0008": "$f_{ij} : V_{ij} \\to V \\times_U U_i \\to V$", "MATH_0009": "$|V| = \\bigcup_{i \\in I} \\bigcup_{j \\in J_i} f_{ij}(|V_{ij}|)$", "MATH_0010": "$|V|$", "MATH_0011": "$|V|$", "MATH_0012": "$V_{i_1j_1}, \\ldots, V_{i_Nj_N}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\{V_{i_kj_k} \\to V\\}_{k = 1, \\ldots, N}$", "MATH_0014": "$V$", "MATH_0015": "$\\{U_i \\times_U V \\to V\\}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth-syntomic-fppf}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{definition-fpqc-covering}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-composition-finite-presentation}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-composition-flat}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-etale-flat}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-etale-locally-finite-presentation}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-fppf-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cea012903a49ef4febb9d0a897b24dec0eff5808981bdf495f4106b58c446034", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:74e973e483514cd110c14dbac4db916768e0a0e965527c67fb8ee513e132a2d1", "source_text": "We will show that an fppf covering is an fpqc covering, and then the\nrest follows from\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0001> be an\nfppf covering of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0002>.\nBy definition this means that the <MATH_0003> are flat which checks the first\ncondition of Definition <REF_0002>. To check the\nsecond, let <MATH_0004> be a morphism with <MATH_0005> affine.\nWe may choose an <ACCENT_0001>tale covering <MATH_0006>\nwith <MATH_0007> affine. Then the compositions\n<MATH_0008> are flat and locally of\nfinite presentation as compositions of such\n(Morphisms of Spaces, Lemmas\n<REF_0003>,\n<REF_0004>,\n<REF_0005>, and\n<REF_0006>).\nHence these morphisms are open\n(Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0007>)\nand we see that\n<MATH_0009>\nis an open covering of <MATH_0010>.\nSince <MATH_0011> is quasi-compact, this covering has a finite\nrefinement.\nSay <MATH_0012> do the job.\nThen <MATH_0013> is\na standard fpqc covering of <MATH_0014> refinining the family\n<MATH_0015>.\nThis finishes the proof.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b8b4eb8f38829dcb2a62b4faf3fdb4e56dd6d1823b2b5646058461aaa51ae67e", "unit_id": "tag:0DFQ:proof"}
